Date: Sat, 22 Aug 2026 09:27:31 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] gatekeeper: device list moves from nvram to /jffs - the
 45-device wall (field report RT-BE88U v2.6.0)

Field report 2026-08-22: after ~45 approved devices every further approve
"succeeded" in the UI and audit log but never persisted; gk_rl stayed at
990 bytes. Root cause: the HND kernel nvram store (bcm_knvram
wlcsm_nvram.c) rejects a name+value tuple over WLCSM_NAMEVALUEPAIR_MAX =
1024 bytes with WLCSM_GEN_ERR and libnvram reports nothing; Merlin's
JFFS_NVRAM escape only covers a name whitelist baked into the prebuilt
libnvram.so, which a Reaper variable cannot join. 22 bytes per entry ->
silent cap at 45.

- shared/gk_rl.c (libshared): gk_rl_get() / gk_rl_set() / gk_rl_migrate().
  Same wire format, stored at /jffs/gatekeeper/rl (0600, tmp+fsync+rename).
  gk_rl_get() falls back to nvram until start_gk migrates once and clears
  the nvram copy; a stale nvram value can never re-shadow the file. Every
  failure path logs "device list NOT saved" - the old path was silent.
- httpd/web.c (4 reads, 2 writes), rc/gatekeeper.c, gkd/gkd.c switched.
  The three nvram_commit() calls after gk_rl_update() dropped (nothing to
  commit; each cost seconds of flash write per click).
- Tables sized for the new ceiling: gkd MAX_DEV 256->512, httpd
  GK_SEEN_MAX 256->512, RDEV_MAX 320->512.
- Settings backup (nvram export) no longer carries the Gatekeeper list;
  factory reset (wipes /jffs) clears it, which is the correct default-deny
  outcome.

Host unit test (stubbed nvram, GK_RL_DIR override): nvram fallback (45
entries), migrate + clear, 300 entries round-trip (6.6 KB), empty set,
stale nvram not re-imported - all pass.
